Packaging wsl-dns-forward for distributions
============================================

Template packaging files are under packaging/ (they are included in the release
tarball):

  packaging/debian/   Debian, Ubuntu and derivatives (debhelper 13, source format 3.0 quilt)
  packaging/alpine/   Alpine Linux APKBUILD
  packaging/arch/     Arch Linux PKGBUILD (installs the daemon to /usr/bin, as Arch merges /usr/sbin)
  packaging/rpm/      Fedora, RHEL and derivatives
  packaging/suse/     openSUSE and SUSE Linux Enterprise

What it is
----------
A small C program (a DNS server for 127.0.0.1:53) plus one PowerShell script
that it sends to powershell.exe through WSL interop.  It exists to make .local
(mDNS) names resolve inside WSL2 on Windows 10.

Build
-----
  ./configure --prefix=/usr --sysconfdir=/etc --localstatedir=/var \
              [--with-systemdsystemunitdir=/usr/lib/systemd/system]
  make
  make check
  make DESTDIR=... install

The release tarball already contains configure.  From a git checkout run
"autoreconf -i" first (autoconf and automake are then build dependencies).

Dependencies
------------
Build:    a C compiler (C11, with accept4 and pipe2: any glibc or musl), make and awk
          (configure needs awk; some minimal container images lack it).
Tests:    dig (Debian: bind9-dnsutils or dnsutils; Fedora/RHEL/SUSE: bind-utils;
          Alpine: bind-tools).  Without dig the integration test is skipped.
Runtime:  none beyond libc.  At run time it needs a WSL system with interop
          enabled and Windows PowerShell on the Windows side.

What gets installed
-------------------
  /usr/sbin/wsl-dns-forward
  /usr/share/wsl-dns-forward/mdns-helper.ps1
  /usr/share/man/man8/wsl-dns-forward.8
  optionally the systemd unit wsl-dns-forward.service

Building a package on your own system
-------------------------------------
Each distribution family can build its package from the release tarball
(wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0.tar.gz) on the machine that will use it, including a
WSL2 distribution.  Run the commands for your family in the directory that holds
the tarball.

Debian, Ubuntu, Kali and derivatives:

  sudo apt install build-essential debhelper dnsutils
  cp wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0.tar.gz wsl-dns-forward_1.0.0.orig.tar.gz
  tar xzf wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0.tar.gz
  cd wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0 && cp -r packaging/debian debian
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
  sudo apt install ../wsl-dns-forward_1.0.0-1_*.deb

Fedora, RHEL, Rocky, AlmaLinux, Oracle Linux (use yum instead of dnf on
Oracle Linux 7):

  sudo dnf install rpm-build gcc make bind-utils systemd-rpm-macros
  mkdir -p ~/rpmbuild/SOURCES ~/rpmbuild/SPECS
  cp wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0.tar.gz ~/rpmbuild/SOURCES/
  tar xzf wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0.tar.gz --strip-components=3 -C ~/rpmbuild/SPECS \
      wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0/packaging/rpm/wsl-dns-forward.spec
  rpmbuild -ba ~/rpmbuild/SPECS/wsl-dns-forward.spec
  sudo dnf install ~/rpmbuild/RPMS/*/wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0-*.rpm

openSUSE and SUSE Linux Enterprise (same steps, with the SUSE spec file):

  sudo zypper install rpm-build gcc make bind-utils systemd-rpm-macros tar gzip
  mkdir -p ~/rpmbuild/SOURCES ~/rpmbuild/SPECS
  cp wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0.tar.gz ~/rpmbuild/SOURCES/
  tar xzf wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0.tar.gz --strip-components=3 -C ~/rpmbuild/SPECS \
      wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0/packaging/suse/wsl-dns-forward.spec
  rpmbuild -ba ~/rpmbuild/SPECS/wsl-dns-forward.spec
  sudo zypper install ~/rpmbuild/RPMS/*/wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0-*.rpm

Arch Linux:

  sudo pacman -S --needed base-devel bind
  mkdir build && cp wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0.tar.gz build/
  tar xzf wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0.tar.gz --strip-components=3 -C build \
      wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0/packaging/arch/PKGBUILD
  cd build && makepkg -si

Alpine Linux (as a user in the abuild group, with a signing key from
"abuild-keygen -a -i"):

  sudo apk add alpine-sdk bind-tools
  mkdir build && cd build
  tar xzf ../wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0.tar.gz --strip-components=3 \
      wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0/packaging/alpine/APKBUILD
  sudo cp ../wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0.tar.gz /var/cache/distfiles/
  abuild checksum && abuild -r
  sudo apk add ~/packages/*/*/wsl-dns-forward-1.0.0-r0.apk

Without a package, "./configure && make && sudo make install" works on all of
them; see INSTALL.

Packaging policy notes
----------------------
* The package must NOT edit /etc/wsl.conf or /etc/resolv.conf in its scripts.
  Both are administrator decisions, and /etc/resolv.conf is often locked.
  Point users at README.md (setup) instead; the Debian template does this
  with README.Debian.
* Do not enable or start the systemd unit automatically.  The normal WSL setup
  starts the daemon from the [boot] command in /etc/wsl.conf.
* The daemon runs as the user "nobody" after opening port 53.  No dedicated
  user is needed.
* The cache directory /var/cache/wsl-dns-forward is created by the daemon at
  start-up.
* Hardening flags (stack protector, PIE, full RELRO, fortify) are added by
  configure and respect the distribution's own CFLAGS.
* The source is plain ASCII C; there are no bundled dependencies.
